From 650986af1971ef45cb0469d71239a663c02f2ea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jatniel <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:55:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the touch layout configuration (positions and safe area)

touch/config.rs keeps what the player changed in touch-layout.json in the game
folder (so each profile has its own): an offset for each control, as a share of
the screen so it holds on iPhone and iPad, plus size, opacity and hidden, which
are read, checked and saved now and applied by the next change. A missing,
empty or broken file is Pocket Edition's layout, unknown controls are ignored
and values out of range are brought into it.

Layout::with_config applies the offsets, keeping each control (the D-pad with
its joystick, the key cap row as one, Chat beside a moved Pause) inside the
screen's safe area, and pushes the margins out from the notch, the rounded
corners and the home indicator where the insets say so. Layout::new is the
default configuration, so every existing layout test still holds, and the
placement now includes the configuration, so a change ends the touches in
progress. The game reads the profile's file once, and again when it moves to
another profile. The window's insets are not plumbed in yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
